I did a mistake with git so I had to close PR #2582

## Change
As discussed in #2404 models tested by an AbstractBaseChatModelIT inheritor can have differents capabilities (often the ligths version doesn't support multimodality : example GPT3.5 does'nt support images).
The idea would be to have
```java
public record ChatLanguageModelCapabilities(
    ChatLanguageModel chatLanguageModel,
    boolean supportsModelNameParameter,
    boolean supportsMaxOutputTokensParameter,
    boolean supportsStopSequencesParameter,
    boolean supportsTemperatureParameter,
    boolean supportsTopPParameter,
    boolean ...
) {}
```

and tests like:

```java
@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("models")
protected void shouldHandleStopSequencesBasedOnModelCapabilities(ChatLanguageModelCapabilities modelCapabilities) {
    if (modelCapabilities.supportsStopSequencesParameter()) {
        // should support stop sequences
    } else {
        // should fail
    }
}
```

The current combination:

```java
@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("models")
@DisabledIf("supportsStopSequencesParameter")
protected void should_fail_if_stopSequences_parameter_is_not_supported(M model) { ... }

@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("models")
@EnabledIf("supportsStopSequencesParameter")
protected void should_respect_stopSequences_in_chat_request(M model) { ... }
```

is not as flexible. The combination of `@EnabledIf` and `@DisabledIf` means either you test models that support the feature or those that don't, but you can't test in the same integration test both models that should fail and those that should pass the test.  


