Support POJOs as `@Tool` method parameters.
Repurpose `@Description` to be used to describe POJO fields.

Example:

```java
@Data
static class Query {

    @Description("List of fields to fetch records")
    List<String> select;

    @Description("List of conditions to filter on. Pass null if no condition")
    List<Condition> where;

    @Description("limit on number of records")
    Integer limit;

    @Description("offset for fetching records")
    Integer offset;
}

@Data
static class Condition {

    @Description("Field to filter on")
    String field;

    @Description("Operator to apply")
    Operator operator;

    @Description("Value to compare with")
    Object value;
}

enum Operator {

    EQUALS,
    NOT_EQUALS,
    IS_NULL,
    IS_NOT_NULL
}

@Tool
public String executeQuery(Query query) {
    ....
}
```

